Why A3 cannot pass (test-side conflict):
A3 (line 557) requires 0 text nodes of every back body to hold "storytime" or "advantage". The
student back and the teacher back render the 5 contact lines of BACK_LINES.contact. Two of those
lines hold the series name as ASCII text. The failure names 2 `contact-line` nodes on the
student-back. A5 keeps the contact block, and spec D-A9 and the print gate (test-strategy.md section
4.10 check 3) require the words "Storytime Advantage" on every back page. So the bodies cannot both
keep the contact block and hold no series name. The fronts pass A3.

Why A8 cannot pass (test-side conflict):
A8 (line 700) calls `parseQuestArgs(['--top', 'hlogo'])` with no --level and no --unit, and expects
errors [] and args not null. A8 (line 705) calls `parseQuestArgs([])` and expects args not null.
Old test B02 (quest-cover-build.test.ts lines 517 to 536) expects an error and args null for
`['--unit', '1']` (no --level), for `['--level', '2']` (no --unit), and for `[]` (no argument). The
same input `[]` has two opposite expectations, so no parser can satisfy both. The flag itself works:
`--top hlogo` sets top hlogo, the default is banner, and `--top round` gives an error with args null.

